-- coa7-ch2.l4: Part 13 Chapter 2, Written resolutions (ss 288 to 300), lines 3786-3886 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Tag conventions are those of coa7-ch1.l4 (FALSE-kind, NOTHING-kind, FORK, MARGINAL).
-- Seams taken as inputs (PLAN.md section 4): `s 1121 the officer is in default` (coa24), `s 168` and `s 510` (coa4, coa12).

§ `Part 13 Chapter 2 -- Written resolutions`

§§ `General provisions about written resolutions`

-- ---- s 288 Written resolutions of private companies --------------------------------------------------------

-- This is the seam answer other parts take as `s 288 the resolution is a written resolution`.
-- src:3789 | (1) In the Companies Acts a “written resolution” means a resolution of a private company proposed and passed in accordance with this Chapter.
@ref s 288(1) Written resolutions of private companies (src:3789)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was proposed in accordance with this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was passed in accordance with this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 288(1) the resolution is a written resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`)
        AND `the resolution was proposed in accordance with this Chapter`
        AND `the resolution was passed in accordance with this Chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“written resolution” means a resolution of a private company proposed and passed in accordance with this Chapter"

-- src:3790 | (2) The following may not be passed as a written resolution—
-- src:3791 | (a) a resolution under section 168 removing a director before the expiration of his period of office;
-- src:3792 | (b) a resolution under section 510 removing an auditor before the expiration of his term of office.
@ref s 288(2) Written resolutions of private companies: what may not be passed as one (src:3790-3792)
GIVEN `s 168 the resolution removes a director before the expiration of his period of office` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 510 the resolution removes an auditor before the expiration of his term of office` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 288(2) the resolution may not be passed as a written resolution` MEANS
    IF `s 168 the resolution removes a director before the expiration of his period of office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `s 510 the resolution removes an auditor before the expiration of his term of office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following may not be passed as a written resolution" names two resolutions and does not say "only"

DECLARE `s 288(3) who proposes the resolution` IS ONE OF
    `s 288(3)(a) the directors of a private company`
    `s 288(3)(b) the members of a private company`
    `s 288(3) another person`

-- src:3793 | (3) A resolution may be proposed as a written resolution—
-- src:3794 | (a) by the directors of a private company (see section 291), or
-- src:3795 | (b) by the members of a private company (see sections 292 to 295).
@ref s 288(3) Written resolutions of private companies: who may propose one (src:3793-3795)
GIVEN proposer IS A `s 288(3) who proposes the resolution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 288(3) the resolution may be proposed as a written resolution by the proposer` MEANS
    CONSIDER proposer
    WHEN `s 288(3)(a) the directors of a private company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 288(3)(b) the members of a private company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 288(3) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A resolution may be proposed as a written resolution— (a) ... or (b) ..." does not say "only"

-- src:3796 | (4) References in enactments passed or made before this Chapter comes into force to—
-- src:3797 | (a) a resolution of a company in general meeting, or
-- src:3798 | (b) a resolution of a meeting of a class of members of the company,
-- src:3799 | have effect as if they included references to a written resolution of the members, or of a class of members, of a private company (as appropriate).
@ref s 288(4) Written resolutions of private companies: older enactments (src:3796-3799)
GIVEN `the enactment was passed or made before this Chapter came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment refers to a resolution of a company in general meeting or of a meeting of a class of members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 288(4) the reference includes a written resolution of the members` MEANS
    IF `the enactment was passed or made before this Chapter came into force`
        AND `the enactment refers to a resolution of a company in general meeting or of a meeting of a class of members`
        AND (NOT `the company is a public company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in enactments passed or made before this Chapter comes into force to— (a) ... (b) ..."

DECLARE `s 288(5) as if passed` IS ONE OF
    `s 288(5)(a) by the company in general meeting`
    `s 288(5)(b) by a meeting of a class of members of the company`

-- src:3800 | (5) A written resolution of a private company has effect as if passed (as the case may be)—
-- src:3801 | (a) by the company in general meeting, or
-- src:3802 | (b) by a meeting of a class of members of the company,
-- src:3803 | and references in enactments passed or made before this section comes into force to a meeting at which a resolution is passed or to members voting in favour of a resolution shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 288(5) Written resolutions of private companies: effect as if passed at a meeting (src:3800-3803)
GIVEN `the resolution is a written resolution of a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is of a class of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 288(5) as if passed`
`s 288(5) the written resolution has effect as if passed` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the resolution is a written resolution of a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A written resolution of a private company has effect as if passed"
    ELSE IF `the resolution is of a class of members`
         THEN JUST `s 288(5)(b) by a meeting of a class of members of the company`
         ELSE JUST `s 288(5)(a) by the company in general meeting`

@ref s 288(5) Written resolutions of private companies: references to a meeting or to voting in favour (src:3803)
GIVEN `the enactment was passed or made before this section came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment refers to a meeting at which a resolution is passed or to members voting in favour of a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 288(5) the reference is construed to include a written resolution` MEANS
    IF `the enactment was passed or made before this section came into force`
        AND `the enactment refers to a meeting at which a resolution is passed or to members voting in favour of a resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "references in enactments passed or made before this section comes into force to a meeting at which a resolution is passed or to members voting in favour of a resolution"

-- ---- s 289 Eligible members --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3805 | (1) In relation to a resolution proposed as a written resolution of a private company, the eligible members are the members who would have been entitled to vote on the resolution on the circulation date of the resolution (see section 290).
@ref s 289(1) Eligible members (src:3805)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution of a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member would have been entitled to vote on the resolution on the circulation date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 289(1) the member is an eligible member` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution of a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to a resolution proposed as a written resolution of a private company"
    ELSE IF `the member would have been entitled to vote on the resolution on the circulation date`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the eligible members are the members who would have been entitled to vote on the resolution on the circulation date"

-- src:3806 | (2) If the persons entitled to vote on a written resolution change during the course of the day that is the circulation date of the resolution, the eligible members are the persons entitled to vote on the resolution at the time that the first copy of the resolution is sent or submitted to a member for his agreement.
@ref s 289(2) Eligible members: entitlement changes during the circulation day (src:3806)
GIVEN `the persons entitled to vote on the written resolution change during the course of the circulation date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was entitled to vote on the resolution at the time the first copy was sent or submitted to a member for his agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 289(2) the person is an eligible member` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the persons entitled to vote on the written resolution change during the course of the circulation date`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the persons entitled to vote on a written resolution change during the course of the day that is the circulation date of the resolution" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the person was entitled to vote on the resolution at the time the first copy was sent or submitted to a member for his agreement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the eligible members are the persons entitled to vote on the resolution at the time that the first copy of the resolution is sent or submitted to a member for his agreement"

-- ---- s 290 Circulation date --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The circulation date: the date copies are sent or submitted to members, or the first of those days.
-- src:3809 | References in this Part to the circulation date of a written resolution are to the date on which copies of it are sent or submitted to members in accordance with this Chapter (or if copies are sent or submitted to members on different days, to the first of those days).
@ref s 290 Circulation date (src:3809)
GIVEN `the days on which copies were sent or submitted to members in accordance with this Chapter` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 290 the circulation date` MEANS
    CONSIDER sort (map (GIVEN d YIELD Day d) `the days on which copies were sent or submitted to members in accordance with this Chapter`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no copy has yet been sent or submitted, so there is no circulation date
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (Date first)

§§ `Circulation of written resolutions`

-- ---- s 291 Circulation of written resolutions proposed by directors ----------------------------------------

-- src:3811 | (1) This section applies to a resolution proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company.
@ref s 291(1) Circulation of written resolutions proposed by directors: application (src:3811)
GIVEN `the resolution was proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 291(1) this section applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution was proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a resolution proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company"

-- src:3812 | (2) The company must send or submit a copy of the resolution to every eligible member.
@ref s 291(2) Circulation of written resolutions proposed by directors: to every eligible member (src:3812)
GIVEN `the resolution was proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligible members` IS A NUMBER
      `eligible members to whom a copy of the resolution was sent or submitted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 291(2) the company has sent or submitted a copy of the resolution to every eligible member` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the resolution was proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a resolution proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company"
    ELSE IF `eligible members to whom a copy of the resolution was sent or submitted` AT LEAST `eligible members`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must send or submit a copy of the resolution to every eligible member" -- FORK F5

DECLARE `s 291(3) manner of circulation` IS ONE OF
    `s 291(3)(a) sending copies at the same time to all eligible members in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website`
    `s 291(3)(b) submitting the same copy (or different copies) to each eligible member in turn`
    `s 291(3) sending copies to some members under (a) and submitting copies to the others under (b)`
    `s 291(3) some other manner`

-- src:3813 | (3) The company must do so—
-- src:3814 | (a) by sending copies at the same time (so far as reasonably practicable) to all eligible members in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website, or
-- src:3815 | (b) if it is possible to do so without undue delay, by submitting the same copy to each eligible member in turn (or different copies to each of a number of eligible members in turn),
-- src:3816 | or by sending copies to some members in accordance with paragraph (a) and submitting a copy or copies to other members in accordance with paragraph (b).
@ref s 291(3) Circulation of written resolutions proposed by directors: the manner (src:3813-3816)
GIVEN manner IS A `s 291(3) manner of circulation`
      `it is possible to submit copies to the members in turn without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 291(3) the manner of circulation is one this section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `s 291(3)(a) sending copies at the same time to all eligible members in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 291(3)(b) submitting the same copy (or different copies) to each eligible member in turn` THEN
        IF `it is possible to submit copies to the members in turn without undue delay`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if it is possible to do so without undue delay, by submitting the same copy to each eligible member in turn"
    WHEN `s 291(3) sending copies to some members under (a) and submitting copies to the others under (b)` THEN
        IF `it is possible to submit copies to the members in turn without undue delay`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or by sending copies to some members in accordance with paragraph (a) and submitting a copy or copies to other members in accordance with paragraph (b)"
    WHEN `s 291(3) some other manner` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must do so— (a) ... or (b) ..." -- FORK F5

-- src:3817 | (4) The copy of the resolution must be accompanied by a statement informing the member—
-- src:3818 | (a) how to signify agreement to the resolution (see section 296), and
-- src:3819 | (b) as to the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse (see section 297).
@ref s 291(4) Circulation of written resolutions proposed by directors: the accompanying statement (src:3817-3819)
GIVEN `the copy is accompanied by a statement informing the member how to signify agreement to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is accompanied by a statement informing the member of the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 291(4) the copy is accompanied by the statement this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the copy is accompanied by a statement informing the member how to signify agreement to the resolution`
        AND `the copy is accompanied by a statement informing the member of the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy of the resolution must be accompanied by a statement informing the member— (a) how to signify agreement to the resolution (see section 296), and (b) as to the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse" -- FORK F5

-- src:3820 | (5) In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 291(5) Circulation of written resolutions proposed by directors: offence (src:3820)
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 291(5) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company is in default in complying with this section`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:3821 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:3822 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:3823 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 291(6) Circulation of written resolutions proposed by directors: penalty (src:3821-3823)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 291(6) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
-- src:3824 | (7) The validity of the resolution, if passed, is not affected by a failure to comply with this section.
@ref s 291(7) Circulation of written resolutions proposed by directors: validity (src:3824)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 291(7) the failure affects the validity of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company failed to comply with this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The validity of the resolution, if passed, is not affected by a failure to comply with this section."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply

-- ---- s 292 Members' power to require circulation of written resolution ------------------------------------

-- src:3827 | (2) Any resolution may properly be moved as a written resolution unless—
-- src:3828 | (a) it would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise),
-- src:3829 | (b) it is defamatory of any person, or
-- src:3830 | (c) it is frivolous or vexatious.
@ref s 292(2) Members' power to require circulation of written resolution: a resolution that may properly be moved (src:3827-3830)
GIVEN `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is defamatory of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 292(2) the resolution may properly be moved as a written resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)`
        OR `the resolution is defamatory of any person`
        OR `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any resolution may properly be moved as a written resolution unless— (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3826 | (1) The members of a private company may require the company to circulate a resolution that may properly be moved and is proposed to be moved as a written resolution.
@ref s 292(1) Members' power to require circulation of written resolution (src:3826)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution may properly be moved as a written resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is proposed to be moved as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 292(1) the members may require the company to circulate the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a private company may require the company to circulate a resolution"
    ELSE IF (NOT `the resolution is proposed to be moved as a written resolution`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a resolution that may properly be moved and is proposed to be moved as a written resolution"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the resolution may properly be moved as a written resolution`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a resolution that may properly be moved" -- MARGINAL b

-- src:3831 | (3) Where the members require a company to circulate a resolution they may require the company to circulate with it a statement of not more than 1,000 words on the subject matter of the resolution.
@ref s 292(3) Members' power to require circulation of written resolution: the statement (src:3831)
GIVEN `words in the statement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 292(3) the members may require the company to circulate a statement of this length with the resolution` MEANS
    IF `words in the statement` AT MOST 1000
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a statement of not more than 1,000 words on the subject matter of the resolution"

-- The requisite percentage, as a fraction: 0.05 is 5%.
-- src:3833 | (5) The “requisite percentage” is 5% or such lower percentage as is specified for this purpose in the company's articles.
@ref s 292(5) Members' power to require circulation of written resolution: the requisite percentage (src:3833)
GIVEN `lower percentage specified for this purpose in the company's articles` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 292(5) the requisite percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `lower percentage specified for this purpose in the company's articles`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 0.05
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        IF p AT MOST 0.05
        THEN JUST p
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "5% or such lower percentage as is specified for this purpose in the company's articles"

-- src:3832 | (4) A company is required to circulate the resolution and any accompanying statement once it has received requests that it do so from members representing not less than the requisite percentage of the total voting rights of all members entitled to vote on the resolution.
@ref s 292(4) Members' power to require circulation of written resolution: when the company is required (src:3832)
GIVEN `fraction of the total voting rights of all members entitled to vote on the resolution held by the members who have requested circulation` IS A NUMBER
      `the requisite percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 292(4) the company is required to circulate the resolution and any accompanying statement` MEANS
    IF `fraction of the total voting rights of all members entitled to vote on the resolution held by the members who have requested circulation` AT LEAST `the requisite percentage`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is required to circulate the resolution and any accompanying statement once it has received requests that it do so from members representing not less than the requisite percentage" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3834 | (6) A request—
-- src:3835 | (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form,
-- src:3836 | (b) must identify the resolution and any accompanying statement, and
-- src:3837 | (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it.
@ref s 292(6) Members' power to require circulation of written resolution: the request (src:3834-3837)
GIVEN `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request identifies the resolution and any accompanying statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 292(6) the request meets the requirements of this subsection` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A request— (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form"
    ELSE IF `the request identifies the resolution and any accompanying statement` AND `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) must identify the resolution and any accompanying statement, and (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 293 Circulation of written resolution proposed by members -------------------------------------------

-- src:3839 | (1) A company that is required under section 292 to circulate a resolution must send or submit to every eligible member—
-- src:3840 | (a) a copy of the resolution, and
-- src:3841 | (b) a copy of any accompanying statement.
-- src:3842 | This is subject to section 294(2) (deposit or tender of sum in respect of expenses of circulation) and section 295 (application not to circulate members' statement).
@ref s 293(1) Circulation of written resolution proposed by members (src:3839-3842)
GIVEN `the company is required under section 292 to circulate the resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 294(2) the company is bound to comply with section 293` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 295(1) the company is not required to circulate the members' statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there is an accompanying statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 293(1) the company must send or submit the copies to every eligible member` MEANS
    IF `the company is required under section 292 to circulate the resolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that is required under section 292 to circulate a resolution must send or submit" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `s 294(2) the company is bound to comply with section 293` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to section 294(2) (deposit or tender of sum in respect of expenses of circulation)" -- FORK F6
         ELSE IF `the company is required under section 292 to circulate the resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 AND `s 294(2) the company is bound to comply with section 293` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 AND ((NOT `there is an accompanying statement`) OR `s 295(1) the company is not required to circulate the members' statement` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 295(1) leaves out only the members' statement, and the answers of ss 292(4) or 294(2) are not known

DECLARE `s 293(2) manner of circulation` IS ONE OF
    `s 293(2)(a) sending copies at the same time to all eligible members in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website`
    `s 293(2)(b) submitting the same copy (or different copies) to each eligible member in turn`
    `s 293(2) sending copies to some members under (a) and submitting copies to the others under (b)`
    `s 293(2) some other manner`

-- src:3843 | (2) The company must do so—
-- src:3844 | (a) by sending copies at the same time (so far as reasonably practicable) to all eligible members in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website, or
-- src:3845 | (b) if it is possible to do so without undue delay, by submitting the same copy to each eligible member in turn (or different copies to each of a number of eligible members in turn),
-- src:3846 | or by sending copies to some members in accordance with paragraph (a) and submitting a copy or copies to other members in accordance with paragraph (b).
@ref s 293(2) Circulation of written resolution proposed by members: the manner (src:3843-3846)
GIVEN manner IS A `s 293(2) manner of circulation`
      `it is possible to submit copies to the members in turn without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 293(2) the manner of circulation is one this section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `s 293(2)(a) sending copies at the same time to all eligible members in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 293(2)(b) submitting the same copy (or different copies) to each eligible member in turn` THEN
        IF `it is possible to submit copies to the members in turn without undue delay`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if it is possible to do so without undue delay, by submitting the same copy to each eligible member in turn"
    WHEN `s 293(2) sending copies to some members under (a) and submitting copies to the others under (b)` THEN
        IF `it is possible to submit copies to the members in turn without undue delay`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or by sending copies to some members in accordance with paragraph (a) and submitting a copy or copies to other members in accordance with paragraph (b)"
    WHEN `s 293(2) some other manner` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must do so— (a) ... or (b) ..." -- FORK F5

-- src:3847 | (3) The company must send or submit the copies (or, if copies are sent or submitted to members on different days, the first of those copies) not more than 21 days after it becomes subject to the requirement under section 292 to circulate the resolution.
@ref s 293(3) Circulation of written resolution proposed by members: within 21 days (src:3847)
GIVEN `the date the company became subject to the requirement under section 292 to circulate the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the date the copies (or the first of them) were sent or submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 293(3) the copies were sent or submitted in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the copies (or the first of them) were sent or submitted` AT MOST `the date the company became subject to the requirement under section 292 to circulate the resolution` PLUS 21
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not more than 21 days after it becomes subject to the requirement under section 292 to circulate the resolution" -- FORK F7

-- src:3848 | (4) The copy of the resolution must be accompanied by guidance as to—
-- src:3849 | (a) how to signify agreement to the resolution (see section 296), and
-- src:3850 | (b) the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse (see section 297).
@ref s 293(4) Circulation of written resolution proposed by members: the guidance (src:3848-3850)
GIVEN `the copy is accompanied by guidance as to how to signify agreement to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is accompanied by guidance as to the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 293(4) the copy is accompanied by the guidance this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the copy is accompanied by guidance as to how to signify agreement to the resolution`
        AND `the copy is accompanied by guidance as to the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy of the resolution must be accompanied by guidance as to— (a) how to signify agreement to the resolution (see section 296), and (b) the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse (see section 297)" -- FORK F5

-- src:3851 | (5) In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 293(5) Circulation of written resolution proposed by members: offence (src:3851)
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 293(5) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company is in default in complying with this section`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:3852 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:3853 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:3854 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 293(6) Circulation of written resolution proposed by members: penalty (src:3852-3854)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 293(6) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
-- src:3855 | (7) The validity of the resolution, if passed, is not affected by a failure to comply with this section.
@ref s 293(7) Circulation of written resolution proposed by members: validity (src:3855)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 293(7) the failure affects the validity of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company failed to comply with this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The validity of the resolution, if passed, is not affected by a failure to comply with this section."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply

-- ---- s 294 Expenses of circulation -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3857 | (1) The expenses of the company in complying with section 293 must be paid by the members who requested the circulation of the resolution unless the company resolves otherwise.
@ref s 294(1) Expenses of circulation (src:3857)
GIVEN `the company has resolved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 294(1) the expenses of complying with section 293 must be paid by the members who requested the circulation` MEANS
    IF `the company has resolved otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be paid by the members who requested the circulation of the resolution unless the company resolves otherwise"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3858 | (2) Unless the company has previously so resolved, it is not bound to comply with that section unless there is deposited with or tendered to it a sum reasonably sufficient to meet its expenses in doing so.
@ref s 294(2) Expenses of circulation: deposit or tender (src:3858)
GIVEN `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is deposited with or tendered to the company a sum reasonably sufficient to meet its expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 294(2) the company is bound to comply with section 293` MEANS
    IF `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- FORK F6
    ELSE IF `there is deposited with or tendered to the company a sum reasonably sufficient to meet its expenses`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- FORK F6
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not bound to comply with that section unless there is deposited with or tendered to it a sum reasonably sufficient to meet its expenses in doing so"

-- ---- s 295 Application not to circulate members' statement -------------------------------------------------

-- src:3860 | (1) A company is not required to circulate a members' statement under section 293 if, on an application by the company or another person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 292 and that section are being abused.
@ref s 295(1) Application not to circulate members' statement (src:3860)
GIVEN `an application was made by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by sections 292 and 293 are being abused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 295(1) the company is not required to circulate the members' statement` MEANS
    IF `an application was made by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved`
        AND `the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by sections 292 and 293 are being abused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not required to circulate a members' statement under section 293 if, on an application by the company or another person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 292 and that section are being abused" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3861 | (2) The court may order the members who requested the circulation of the statement to pay the whole or part of the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on such an application, even if they are not parties to the application.
@ref s 295(2) Application not to circulate members' statement: costs (src:3861)
GIVEN `an application was made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 295(2) the court may order the members who requested the circulation to pay the company's costs` MEANS
    IF `an application was made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on such an application, even if they are not parties to the application"

§§ `Agreeing to written resolutions`

-- ---- s 296 Procedure for signifying agreement to written resolution ----------------------------------------

-- src:3864 | (1) A member signifies his agreement to a proposed written resolution when the company receives from him (or from someone acting on his behalf) an authenticated document—
-- src:3865 | (a) identifying the resolution to which it relates, and
-- src:3866 | (b) indicating his agreement to the resolution.
@ref s 296(1) Procedure for signifying agreement to written resolution (src:3864-3866)
GIVEN `the company has received a document from the member or from someone acting on his behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is authenticated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document identifies the resolution to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document indicates the member's agreement to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 296(1) the member has signified agreement to the proposed written resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company has received a document from the member or from someone acting on his behalf`
        AND `the document is authenticated`
        AND `the document identifies the resolution to which it relates`
        AND `the document indicates the member's agreement to the resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A member signifies his agreement to a proposed written resolution when the company receives from him (or from someone acting on his behalf) an authenticated document" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3867 | (2) The document must be sent to the company in hard copy form or in electronic form.
@ref s 296(2) Procedure for signifying agreement to written resolution: the form (src:3867)
GIVEN `the document is sent to the company in hard copy form or in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 296(2) the document is sent in a form this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the document is sent to the company in hard copy form or in electronic form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The document must be sent to the company in hard copy form or in electronic form" -- FORK F5

-- src:3868 | (3) A member's agreement to a written resolution, once signified, may not be revoked.
@ref s 296(3) Procedure for signifying agreement to written resolution: no revocation (src:3868)
GIVEN `the member's agreement has been signified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 296(3) the member's agreement may be revoked` MEANS
    IF `the member's agreement has been signified`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A member's agreement to a written resolution, once signified, may not be revoked"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "once signified"

-- The required majority is that of s 282(2) for an ordinary resolution and s 283(2) for a special resolution.
-- src:3869 | (4) A written resolution is passed when the required majority of eligible members have signified their agreement to it.
@ref s 296(4) Procedure for signifying agreement to written resolution: when it is passed (src:3869)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of resolution`
      counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 296(4) the written resolution is passed` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an ordinary resolution` THEN `s 282(2) a written resolution is passed by a simple majority` counts
    WHEN `a special resolution` THEN `s 283(2) a written resolution is passed by a majority of not less than 75%` counts

-- ---- s 297 Period for agreeing to written resolution -------------------------------------------------------

-- The period "beginning with the circulation date" counts the circulation date as its first day, so 28 days end 27 days later.
-- src:3871 | (1) A proposed written resolution lapses if it is not passed before the end of—
-- src:3872 | (a) the period specified for this purpose in the company's articles, or
-- src:3873 | (b) if none is specified, the period of 28 days beginning with the circulation date.
@ref s 297(1) Period for agreeing to written resolution: the last day (src:3871-3873)
GIVEN `the circulation date` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period specified in the company's articles ends` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 297(1) the last day of the period for agreeing to the written resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the period specified in the company's articles ends`
    WHEN JUST articlesEnd THEN articlesEnd
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the circulation date` PLUS 27

@ref s 297(1) Period for agreeing to written resolution: lapse (src:3871-3873)
GIVEN `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the required majority had signified agreement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day for which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 297(1) the proposed written resolution lapses` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the required majority had signified agreement`
    WHEN JUST passedOn THEN
        IF passedOn AT MOST `the last day of the period`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A proposed written resolution lapses if it is not passed before the end of"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day for which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A proposed written resolution lapses if it is not passed before the end of" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3874 | (2) The agreement of a member to a written resolution is ineffective if signified after the expiry of that period.
@ref s 297(2) Period for agreeing to written resolution: late agreement (src:3874)
GIVEN `the day on which the member's agreement was signified` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 297(2) the member's agreement is ineffective` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the member's agreement was signified` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The agreement of a member to a written resolution is ineffective if signified after the expiry of that period" -- MARGINAL a

§§ `Supplementary`

-- ---- s 298 Sending documents relating to written resolutions by electronic means ---------------------------

-- src:3877 | (1) Where a company has given an electronic address in any document containing or accompanying a proposed written resolution, it is deemed to have agreed that any document or information relating to that resolution may be sent by electronic means to that address (subject to any conditions or limitations specified in the document).
@ref s 298(1) Sending documents relating to written resolutions by electronic means (src:3877)
GIVEN `the company has given an electronic address in a document containing or accompanying the proposed written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information relates to that resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 298(1) the company is deemed to have agreed that the document or information may be sent by electronic means to the address` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has given an electronic address in a document containing or accompanying the proposed written resolution`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company has given an electronic address in any document containing or accompanying a proposed written resolution" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF (NOT `the document or information relates to that resolution`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any document or information relating to that resolution" -- MARGINAL a
         ELSE IF `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the document`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(subject to any conditions or limitations specified in the document)"

-- src:3878 | (2) In this section “electronic address” means any address or number used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means.
@ref s 298(2) Sending documents relating to written resolutions by electronic means: "electronic address" (src:3878)
GIVEN `the address or number is used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 298(2) the address or number is an electronic address` MEANS
    IF `the address or number is used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“electronic address” means any address or number used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means"

-- ---- s 299 Publication of written resolution on website ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:3880 | (1) This section applies where a company sends—
-- src:3881 | (a) a written resolution, or
-- src:3882 | (b) a statement relating to a written resolution,
-- src:3883 | to a person by means of a website.
@ref s 299(1) Publication of written resolution on website: application (src:3880-3883)
GIVEN `the company sends a written resolution, or a statement relating to a written resolution, to a person by means of a website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 299(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company sends a written resolution, or a statement relating to a written resolution, to a person by means of a website`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company sends— (a) a written resolution, or (b) a statement relating to a written resolution, to a person by means of a website" -- MARGINAL a

-- TRUE says the bar holds (it is not validly sent); FALSE says the bar does not apply (the text does not say it is
-- validly sent, only that it is not invalidly sent by this subsection) (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d), an "unless" bar).
-- src:3884 | (2) The resolution or statement is not validly sent for the purposes of this Chapter unless the resolution is available on the website throughout the period beginning with the circulation date and ending on the date on which the resolution lapses under section 297.
@ref s 299(2) Publication of written resolution on website: validity (src:3884)
GIVEN `the company sends the resolution or statement to a person by means of a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is available on the website throughout the period beginning with the circulation date and ending on the date on which it lapses under section 297` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 299(2) the resolution or statement is not validly sent for the purposes of this Chapter` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company sends the resolution or statement to a person by means of a website`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person by means of a website"
    ELSE IF `the resolution is available on the website throughout the period beginning with the circulation date and ending on the date on which it lapses under section 297`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not validly sent for the purposes of this Chapter unless the resolution is available on the website throughout the period" -- FORK F8
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 300 Relationship between this Chapter and provisions of company's articles --------------------------

-- src:3886 | A provision of the articles of a private company is void in so far as it would have the effect that a resolution that is required by or otherwise provided for in an enactment could not be proposed and passed as a written resolution.
@ref s 300 Relationship between this Chapter and provisions of company's articles (src:3886)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision would have the effect that a resolution required by or otherwise provided for in an enactment could not be proposed and passed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 300 the provision of the articles is void` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A provision of the articles of a private company is void"
    ELSE IF `the provision would have the effect that a resolution required by or otherwise provided for in an enactment could not be proposed and passed as a written resolution`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect"
